# REQUIRES: verilator
# Folded port bundles (--fold-ports REGEX, --fold-ports-reset INPUT): the
# netlist ports mp_<k>_<field> of four bundles leave and come as two record
# streams. A bundle's outputs of a target cycle are one request record
# (req_valid / req_ready / req_chan / req_treset / req_bits, the fields low
# first in netlist order), its inputs one response record (rsp_valid /
# rsp_ready / rsp_chan / rsp_bits). The outputs' token queues are memories
# indexed by bundle and entry, written at each field's pushes one bundle a
# host cycle (the pushes of a field spread: @4, 5, 6, 7), a record offered a
# host cycle after the bundle's last push, an early field's token from reset
# zero, the frame's reset token stored beside the record. The kernel's
# header gives the layouts (FOLDSIM_PORTS_*). Against the target with a
# memory-like endpoint on each bundle (Inputs/tb_ports.sv: every bundle
# busy every cycle, answers 1 to 400 host cycles late, in random bundle
# order, channels stalled, bubbles), plain and with spec groups (each
# response field two copies, for the cycle before's fire or not).
# Mutants that fail it: a field's pushes not spread (two bundles' tokens in
# one host cycle: MISMATCH), a record sent once any field is pushed (ORDER /
# MISMATCH), the reset token not carried (MISMATCH).
# RUN: rm -rf %t && mkdir -p %t && cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/ports
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/off --static --nest --modulo Unit > %t/off.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=OFF --implicit-check-not=FOLDSIM_PORTS < %t/off/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/on --static --nest --modulo --fold-ports 'mp_([0-9]+)_(.*)' --fold-ports-reset rst Unit > %t/on.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=VH < %t/on/foldsim_sim.vh
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SLOT < %t/on/schedule.txt
# RUN: %verilator --binary --timing -Wno-fatal -Wno-lint --x-initial unique --top-module tb -I%t/on -Mdir %t/on/obj %S/Inputs/tb_ports.sv top.sv %t/on/foldsim_sim.sv > %t/on/build.log 2>&1
